<title>SRI LANKA: Sri Lanka T-bill yields edge up in auction.</title>
<headline>Sri Lanka T-bill yields edge up in auction.</headline>
<dateline>COLOMBO 1996-09-11</dateline>
<text>
<p>The average yields of three, six and 12-month Sri Lankan treasury bills rose at Wednesday's auctions from those of last week, the Central Bank said.</p>
<p>		  bids received   bids accepted   avg yield</p>
<p>    3 months     5,352	     3,619	 16.98 (16.89)</p>
<p>    6 months	 305		 300	 17.12 (17.07)</p>
<p>   12 months     1,351	     1,121	 17.18 (17.13)</p>
<p>The Central Bank said it bought treasury bills totalling 487 million rupees.</p>
<p>NOTE - Bids in million rupees, yields in percent (previous week's yields in brackets). --Colombo newsroom (941) 434319</p>
</text>
